# This folder is checked out and copied straight onto a Kindle, so every file
# in it has to arrive byte for byte as it was built -- the device scripts verify
# SHA256SUMS before they load anything.
#
# On Windows with core.autocrlf=true (the default of the Git for Windows
# installer, and set on the laptop this port is built from) a text file is
# checked out with CRLF. That was tested on 2026-11-23 with the sparse clone
# this folder's README recommends: SHA256SUMS came out CRLF, every name in it
# gained a trailing \r, and `sha256sum -c` failed on all seven files -- the step
# the instructions tell the reader to trust before copying anything to the
# device. menu.json would be worse: KUAL parses it on the Kindle.
#
# The binaries are already safe (Git does not touch what it detects as binary)
# and ports/koa2/.gitattributes pins *.sh, but SHA256SUMS, menu.json, config.xml
# and the two READMEs were covered by nothing.
* -text
*.md text eol=lf
